# .spun get bomb01 (mame-bomb.sh): BOMB.BIN says it unpacks to 100 bytes but
# inflates to 8 MB. The unzipper must stop as soon as the output passes 100
# bytes, with UNZIP_E_CHECK, not write the 8 MB first, so .spun must end well
# within the run. y at 16 s answers "Install to C:/apps/bomb?". ON ERROR keeps
# the autoexec running when .spun ends with an error, as it must. The handler
# prints SPUNERR with the error code and the line of .spun (30); the PRINT of
# line 40 runs only if .spun returns without an error. screen 29 SPUNERR 255 30
# therefore means that .spun ended with an error before 29 s. It has no
# noreset: NextZXOS fetches $0000 once when a handler catches the error of a
# dot command, with BASIC at the line of that command.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart ON ERROR ERROR TO e,l:PRINT "SPUNERR ";e;" ";l:FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
autostart .spun -s @HOST@ -p @PORT@ get bomb01
autostart PRINT "SPUNBOMBDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 30
key 16 y
snap 14 17 19 22 25 29
screen 29 Installing to C:/apps/bomb
screen 29 SPUNERR 255 30
